 "title": "JUB1-X Synthetase and Related Genes and Proteins",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around JUB1-X synTF, a synthetase that produces PAPS and induces IPTG. It is derived from JUB1 and expresses APSK and ATPS. JUB1 is a protein that recruits RNAP and has a variant JUB1-X. The cluster also includes various genes and proteins related to JUB1 and JUB1-X, such as PPA, PPK, and PPK2CpaN, which are involved in the production of PAPS. Additionally, the cluster includes organisms like Ashbya gossypii, Aspergillus nidulans, and Kluyveromyces lactis, which are associated with these genes and proteins.",
